6. Expense and GST Calculation Engine
6.1 Calculation Modes

The system must support:

Automatic GST calculation.
Manual GST entry.
GST-inclusive pricing.
GST-exclusive pricing.
CGST and SGST.
IGST.
Zero-rated or no-GST purchases where applicable.
Custom tax rates.
Invoice-level rounding adjustments.
6.2 GST Rates

The application should allow configurable rates, including:

0%
5%
12%
18%
28%
Custom rates

The applicable rate must be determined from the product/service classification and tax treatment.

6.3 GST-Exclusive Formula

Taxable Amount:

Quantity × Unit Price

GST Amount:

Taxable Amount × GST Rate / 100

Final Amount:

Taxable Amount + GST Amount

6.4 GST-Inclusive Formula

Taxable Amount:

Inclusive Amount / (1 + GST Rate / 100)

GST Amount:

Inclusive Amount - Taxable Amount

6.5 Intra-State GST

When applicable:

CGST = GST / 2
SGST = GST / 2
6.6 Inter-State GST

When applicable:

IGST = Total GST

The system must determine the tax type from the relevant supplier and recipient state information and allow authorized correction.

6.7 Manual GST Mode

Users must be able to enter invoice values directly.

Fields:

Taxable amount.
CGST.
SGST.
IGST.
Other tax or adjustment.
Final invoice amount.

The system must compare manual values with calculated values and flag differences.

It must never silently overwrite invoice values.

6.8 Financial Precision

Financial calculations must use decimal-safe arithmetic.

Currency values must be stored to appropriate precision.
Exchange rates must preserve sufficient decimal places.
Tax rounding must be configurable.
Historical amounts must not be recalculated when settings change.

The original invoice amount must always be preserved.

7. Currency Conversion
7.1 Supported Currencies
INR
USD
Additional currencies configurable by administrator.
7.2 Conversion Formula

INR Amount:

Original Currency Amount × Transaction Exchange Rate

Example:

USD amount: $44
Exchange rate: ₹90.22
INR equivalent: ₹3,969.68
7.3 Requirements
Store original currency.
Store original amount.
Store transaction exchange rate.
Store converted INR amount.
Preserve historical exchange rates.
Support manual exchange rate entry.
Optionally retrieve current exchange rates from a trusted provider.
Never automatically change previously saved transaction values.

Bank charges and foreign exchange fees should be recorded separately when available.

Foreign software subscriptions must support applicable import-of-services tax treatment without assuming ordinary domestic GST handling.

