33. Final Product Definition

The IT Expense & Resource Management System must function as a centralized financial and operational management platform for the IT department.

It must combine:

Expense management.
Individual category tracking.
Centralized transaction management.
Automatic bill extraction.
GST and currency calculations.
Invoice management.
Approval workflows.
Vendor management.
Inventory management.
Asset management.
Subscription management.
Payment tracking.
Financial reporting.
Excel integration.
Audit history.
Notifications.
Secure online and local access.

The most important requirement is that all modules must work from the same centralized MongoDB data.

A new purchase should be entered or uploaded once, and all relevant category pages, transaction records, inventory information, vendor histories, subscription records and dashboards should update according to the transaction's actual status.

The application must preserve historical data, maintain financial accuracy and provide a reliable record of every IT department purchase.

Final development principle: Build one integrated system, not multiple disconnected expense spreadsheets.